  "result": "No additional blocking interface or public-write defect found. Actual local1024flat-owner operator batches completed in two transactions; source freshness, worst-case leveraged position gas and public timing remain separate evidence boundaries.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "LIVE-ARMED-FINALITY-BUDGET",
      "severity": "proof-reliability",
      "status": "implementation-reviewed-awaiting-clock-aligned-fresh-proof",
      "files": [
        "oracle/services/local-integration/src/live-actors.ts",
        "packages/pricefeed/scripts/live-factory-integration.ts"
      ],
      "detail": "Actor requires matching pause acknowledgement strictly before epoch end. Publisher requires a genuine valid sample captured at or after E-15, sealed before E, and finalized before acknowledgment. Observed capture-to-seal lag is approximately 8-19 seconds plus four-block finality, so the target has insufficient reliable scheduling margin. Some fast paths are possible; success is not guaranteed. No core TTL or finality change is justified by this evidence.",
      "requiredResolution": "Retain unchanged 30-second carry and canonical finality; coordinate driver sequencing optimization and focused regressions before claiming reproducible mature rollover. Preserve original activation deadline and diagnostic run provenance.",
      "activeDiagnosticRun": "tmp/local-live-leverage-20261005-212226",
      "diagnosticDisposition": {
        "run": "tmp/local-live-leverage-20261005-212226",
        "status": "superseded-gracefully-no-completed-proof",
        "marker": "tmp/local-live-leverage-20261005-212226/superseded.json",
        "markerSha256": "5c9646f416cedc4567b1c9059fe06e68206a4a42c34f73e64d600adb3d60d53f"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "BOOTSTRAP-MULTIPAGE-ROLLOVER-LIVENESS",
      "severity": "deployment-readiness",
      "status": "local-flat-capacity-measured-warm-source-and-worst-case-timing-unproven",
      "files": [
        "contracts/src/engine/RiskAccountingBridge.sol",
        "contracts/src/risk/EpochRollover.sol",
        "contracts/src/pricing/RiskPricing.sol",
        "contracts/src/engine/BookRiskEngine.sol",
        "oracle/services/market-ops/src/operations.ts"
      ],
      "detail": "The engine exposes only separate beginRollover, rollPage(max 32), and finishRollover entrypoints. There is no atomic rollover/multicall entrypoint. The frozen sweepCutoff protects account accrual; opening price candidates are recomputed at finish block.timestamp, not frozen at begin. Effective SWEEP after epoch end makes new executable book depth unavailable. A bootstrap market therefore needs the last pre-boundary valid PERP/BASIS sample to remain fresh until finish. With 1,024 owners, 32 pages plus begin/finish exceed the 30-second carry under the configured 1-second block/four-block-finality serial operator. Accounting can still complete safely, but successful small-owner warm rollover does not prove large-market bootstrap liveness.",
      "guarantees": "Missing windows leave pricingMode BOOTSTRAP and prevent leveraged admission. Once NORMAL_PRICING has been reached, the mode does not demote; unavailable mark still disables leveraged admission until windows rebuild. No stale mark is silently accepted.",
      "requiredResolution": "The optional reviewed helper now composes bounded current-gas batches without changing economic contracts. Complete actual operator RPC/finality timing and a clock-aligned warm source proof before claiming reproducible opening liveness; retain the30-second carry and stale-window fallback. The original no-helper scale finding remains valid for legacy3step operators.",
      "gasEvidenceCaution": "Historical gas-engine report has approximately 3.70M Prague / 2.08M Monad gas for a worst 32-owner page; it is not a current batch certificate and does not establish that all 32 pages fit 30M.",
      "sourceReviewAt": "2026-10-05T22:09:43.383281+00:00",
      "resolutionProgressAt": "2026-10-05T22:49:36.894459+00:00",
      "localCapacityEvidence": {
        "path": "artifacts/integration/rollover-rpc-2026-10-06.json",
        "sha256": "e9b009a9d773c01e521d52a0739e9282ba2d0f63384615cbc619270c8d77fd8e",
        "batches": 2,
        "finishSeconds": 13,
        "finalizedMs": 17275
      }
    }
  ],
  "checks": [
    {
      "area": "Browser boundary",
      "result": "Browser entry exports only ABI, typed trading/read builders and sanitized manifest schema. It has no filesystem, environment-key or wallet-signing loader."
    },
    {
      "area": "Read API identity and privacy",
      "result": "Loopback-only listener and exact CORS origins; GET-only endpoints. Chain, runtime code, listing and registry relationships are checked with block-pinned reads. Canonical block hash is rechecked; arbitrary owner reads are bounded. Public manifest serialization strips RPC and unknown fields. HTTP transport errors return controlled messages."
    },
    {
      "area": "Units and unavailable states",
      "result": "Handoff distinguishes lots, token atoms, WAD and Q; stale/unavailable prices remain null. Claims require enabled preparation and positive claimable amount. Owner-specific simulation remains required before wallet sending."
    },
    {
      "area": "Owner transaction and gas",
      "result": "Typed owner and wallet-chain validation precedes building requests. Local actors use measured gas with explicit caps, simulation, chain binding, and exact signed-byte replay. Market-ops refuses untracked pending nonce and binds journals to deployment and sender."
    },
    {
      "area": "Replay limitations",
      "result": "Pending signed transactions can reconcile exactly; partially completed funding and fill-before-summary states do not automatically resume. Fresh-run SDK smoke has no durable signed pending journal and is evidence tooling, not a production resumable workflow."
    },
    {
      "area": "Public write boundary",
      "result": "Public preflight RPC has an explicit read-method allowlist and loads no keys. Mutating rehearsal methods require loopback verified Anvil and a snapshot restored on completion/failure. Upstream fork proxy keeps the public transport read-only. Local harness verifies child and free port, uses sanitized environment, and owns unique evidence directories."
    },
    {
      "area": "Concrete factory deployment",
      "result": "Two STOP-prefixed bytecode stores, expected creation hash, factory/vault/engine CREATE addresses, registry/factory/engine/vault bindings, reciprocal oracle/treasury/token/governance reads, reserve funding and governed activation are checked. Predicted/ephemeral addresses are not presented as deployed public manifests."
    },
    {
      "area": "Wallet roles",
      "result": "Preflight reports role membership and available balances but explicitly does not assert signer custody. Fork impersonation/native gas top-up is labeled; token funds are not fabricated."
    },
    {
      "area": "Closure proof",
      "result": "Watcher stops and drains before sampling lock and settlement start. Auditor independently derives full owner claims from frozen balances, verifies exact owner-paid receipts/events and terminal states, and checks reserve/dust/deficit and custody identities at canonical pinned blocks."
    },
    {
      "area": "Live evidence",
      "result": "Independent live auditor pins actual owner positions/cash/coverage to canonical blocks and checks post-fill capture time, not merely a later seal receipt. Active run remains incomplete; timing finding is retained separately."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This is a code review and retained-test evidence check, not a formal audit, external approval, or full proof of absence of secrets.",
    "Legacy explicit public E2E scenario and generic market-ops broadcast commands still exist for authorized operators; they were not executed by this review. New local/preflight commands are separately constrained.",
    "User-provided provenance labels are metadata, not independently certified source truth. Current code/listing identity is verified; historical verifiedAt metadata is not a substitute for a canonical current snapshot.",
    "SDK smoke verifies loopback chain 31337, fixture token alias and enrolled code/listing identity; its standalone helper does not itself check web3_clientVersion. Root local orchestration does verify and own Anvil.",
    "No wallet-custody, public activation, empirical risk calibration, or paid provider claim follows from local fixture or impersonated fork results.",
    "Review source hashes describe files at review time; later driver corrections need a supplemental review and hashes before release.",
    "Raw local logs and source endpoints are retained under ignored tmp; the browser manifest and versioned review record contain no RPC secrets."
  ],
